    airo:evidenceText "Uber withdrew its self-driving cars from San Francisco a week later, after the California DMV revoked the vehicles’ registrations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b85f7d2f6db> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[987] Uber withdrew its self-driving cars from San Francisco a week later, after the California DMV revoked the vehicles’ registrations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e86aee9d01a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This is why we believe so much in making the roads safer by building self-driving Ubers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "989" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/332b8311b90d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[989] Uber’s San Francisco trial run of its self-driving service last Tuesday is catching people’s attention." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "989" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3cf50412dedd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In May, the “autopilot sensors” on a Tesla Motors car failed to distinguish a white tractor-trailer crossing the highway against a bright sky, leading to the first known death caused by a self-driving car." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "990" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3d98b26a45b5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "in both instances, the vehicles seemed to be the Volvo XC90, launched the same day as Uber’s test run." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "989" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/415146f90406> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[989] This is why we believe so much in making the roads safer by building self-driving Ubers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "989" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/48e7acb0b844> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber's Self-Driving Car Runs Red Light in San Francisco" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/50de748d2d60> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The supposedly human-caused red-light violation, they said, “is why we believe so much in making the roads safer by building self-driving Ubers.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5190a8cbc9c7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Worse still, the apparently flawed system was deployed against explicit demands by California state regulators that they cease operations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/58026b1e28d4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Spokeswoman Chelsea Kohler declined to provide details about Koff’s claims and sent the Guardian a statement identical to the one she provided last week, citing “human error”, adding: “This is why we believe so much in making the roads safer by building self-driving Ubers.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "990" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/776142c5515c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Continuing a week-plus of embarrassments and bad news for Uber, the New York Times on Friday reported that traffic violations by the company’s self-driving cars were caused by problems with the cars’ mapping programs." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/89edb6da604d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The incident was also witnessed by San Fransico writer and producer Annie Guas as she was travelling by a (human piloted) Lyft." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "989" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c305454ca8e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Being able to understand the traffic signal and respond appropriately is a key requirement of any so-called self-driving technology,” said Simpson, who has called for criminal charges again" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "990" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c73e0798e1e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[988] Even if it was a human at the wheel, it’s bad news on the day Uber announced it’s welcoming passengers aboard its fleet of driverless cars in the city, and that it’s doing so without filing for an autonomous testing permit with the California DMV." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aa2c9078150f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber withdrew its self-driving cars from San Francisco a week later, after the California DMV revoked the vehicles’ registrations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0905e9203db> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[988] An Uber equipped to drive itself ran a red light in San Francisco’s SOMA neighborhood Wednesday morning, per a YouTube video apparently shot from a local Luxor cab and reported by The Examiner." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ba66ef88449e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But Uber has ignored attorney general Kamala Harris’s threat of legal action, claiming it does not need permits since the vehicles have drivers monitoring and citing the cars’ “state-of-the-art” technology and “core safety capabilities”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "990" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bcf88bc44329> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Witness says self-driving Uber ran red light on its own, disputing Uber's claims" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "990" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c2d18531e855> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In the video, a Volvo XC90 SUV decked out in the sensors Uber uses to see the world plowed through the intersection roughly three seconds after the light went red, and as a pedestrian was stepping into the crosswalk." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "988" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c3f6cec7de7e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber’s Self-Driving Cars Missed Six Red Lights In San Francisco" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "987" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c72f4a90a856> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "John M Simpson, privacy project director for Consumer Watchdog, who filed a report based on Koff’s incident, said he suspects Uber does not want to follow regulations that would require it to disclose details about errors to the government." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "990" .

